## Changes in this patch

**`button.jsx`** — comments only. The three fenced `@example` regions became indented, unfenced examples; all documented usages are retained and a note records why. No executable line changed, so all 16 existing assertions hold.

**`button.test.jsx`** — two small hardening fixes: `vi` is now explicitly imported rather than relying on `globals: true` in the Vitest config, and the previously assertion-free `forwards ref` test now actually asserts `ref.current` is an `HTMLButtonElement`. That test would have passed even if ref forwarding were broken.

I could not execute the suite from this environment, so the resolution is verified by static reasoning: the truncation trigger is removed, which is a necessary and sufficient fix for the esbuild transform error and the two cascading suite failures. The Base44 network errors in `aiEngine.test.js` and `dataScanner.test.js` are untouched and remain outstanding.